1
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:03,690
Previously on The Big Bang Theory.

2
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:05,440
We were worried about you.

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:07,720
Don't be melodramatic.

4
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:10,530
I'm just getting on a train and leaving forever.

5
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:14,660
So a few things don't go your way

6
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:15,710
and your best decision

7
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:18,200
is to ride the rails like a hobo?

8
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:21,120
Leonard, I am overwhelmed.

9
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:22,270
Everything is changing,

10
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:24,260
and it's simply too much.

11
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,210
I need to get away and think.

12
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:28,140
Sheldon...

13
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:29,880
Yes?

14
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,750
I'm gonna miss you.

15
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:33,730
Of course you are.

16
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,430
You just made that easier.

17
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,990
Excuse me.

18
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:48,840
Is it at all possible

19
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,910
that you're knitting a pair of pants?

20
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:55,250
Oh, well, no, you're understandably terrified.

21
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:57,320
But, you know, allow me to explain.

22
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:00,640
45 days ago, um, I embarked on

23
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,530
a railroad journey of healing

24
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,130
because my university

25
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:05,640
was making me do string theory,

26
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,860
and my favorite comic book store burned down,

27
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,910
and when my roommate got engaged,

28
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:11,880
my girlfriend wanted to move in with me,

29
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,940
which was no doubt a ploy just to see my--

30
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:19,100
well, excuse my language, but my bathing suit parts.

31
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:23,260
Uh, sir, may I use your phone?

32
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:25,250
- I don't think so. - Yeah, well,

33
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,930
I understand that I'm half naked,

34
00:01:26,930 --> 00:01:28,910
but there is a reasonable explanation.

35
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:31,540
While I slept in my sleeper car,

36
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,490
all my possessions were stolen.

37
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:35,930
Now, typically, I wear pajamas,

38
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:39,880
but I recently adopted a hobo lifestyle

39
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:43,330
and pajamas are the sleep-pants of the man.

40
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,520
I'll have you know, Mahatma Gandhi wore no pants

41
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:50,820
and a nation rallied behind him!

42
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,410
My good man...

43
00:01:52,410 --> 00:01:53,580
Now, before you walk away...

44
00:01:53,670 --> 00:01:55,430
I know that I may appear deranged,

45
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:58,130
but I am, in fact, a world-renowned physicist.

46
00:01:58,130 --> 00:02:01,200
Ask me the difference between a boson and a fermion.

47
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,760
Go ahead, ask!

48
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,300
Bosons have integer spin,

49
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,470
fermions have half-integer spin!

50
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:10,960
My legs are getting cold!

51
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:13,150
Why won't anybody help me?

52
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:41,680
Morning.

53
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,500
Hi. Want to do yoga with me?

54
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,540
Um, let me just have some coffee first,

55
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,000
and then I'll have the strength to tell you

56
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,070
how much I won't be doing that.

57
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:53,790
Hello?

58
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,240
Hello, Leonard.

59
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:57,760
Hey, buddy. Good to hear your voice.

60
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:00,220
Uh, I'm in Kingman, Arizona,

61
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:03,280
and, uh, I need you to come pick me up.

62
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:05,370
I'd love to.

63
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:07,980
I'm just about to do yoga with Penny.

64
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:11,850
Leonard, I'm at the police station.

65
00:03:11,850 --> 00:03:12,940
I was robbed.

66
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,250
Th-They took my phone,

67
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:16,630
my wallet, my iPad, everything.

68
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:18,230
Oh, my God, are you okay?

69
00:03:18,230 --> 00:03:19,600
No, I'm not okay.

70
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,840
I-I'm wearing borrowed pants,

71
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,710
I-I don't have I.D.,

72
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:25,220
and one of the officers here

73
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:27,590
won't stop calling me Chicken Legs.

74
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,170
Okay.

75
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:30,280
Uh, I'll-I'll come get you.

76
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:30,980
What's the address?

77
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:32,110
Hey, what's going on?

78
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:33,640
He got all of his stuff stolen.

79
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:36,260
Okay...

80
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,310
Hurry.

81
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:38,620
Sheldon, hang tight.

82
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:40,040
Hey, do you want me to bring anything?

83
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:41,250
Oh, yes, please.

84
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,430
A pair of pants.

85
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:43,690
And my toothbrush.

86
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,430
Yeah, and my mail.

87
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:47,360
And a really good comeback for chicken legs,

88
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:49,560
because "I know you are, but what am I?"

89
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,120
was met with stony silence.

90
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,290
I'll be there as soon as I can.

91
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:55,130
Is he okay?

92
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:57,130
Yeah, he's fine, he's just a little rattled.

93
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,940
Oh... Feel like driving to Arizona with me?

94
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:00,280
I can't, I have that job interview.

95
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,680
Oh, right. Besides,

96
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,210
I don't need six hours of "Your hair is different.

97
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:04,580
Why did you change your hair?

98
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,900
I'm holding my breath until your hair grows back."

99
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,220
All right, fine.

100
00:04:10,670 --> 00:04:11,700
Hey, can you think of a reason

101
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:14,210
- I shouldn't invite Amy to come with me? - Nope.

102
00:04:14,210 --> 00:04:16,350
Come on, you didn't even try.

103
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:20,240
Thanks for the lift.

104
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,590
What's wrong with your car?

105
00:04:21,590 --> 00:04:24,670
I'm having my windows untinted.

106
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:26,730
Why?

107
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:27,700
Got a hot girlfriend now.

108
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,930
I want the haters to know.

109
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,220
What are you talking about?

110
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:33,130
No one's paying attention to you.

111
00:04:34,430 --> 00:04:36,910
How's that Hater-ade taste, bro?

112
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,680
Hey, this isn't the way to work.

113
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,820
I just want to pop in and make sure Ma's okay.

114
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,520
I thought Stuart was looking after her.

115
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:48,040
He was, but now that her cast is off, he moved out.

116
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,360
And honestly, I'm kind of glad.

117
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,010
It was getting a little weird.

118
00:04:51,010 --> 00:04:52,220
How so?

119
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,360
I don't know, they're...

120
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:55,920
chummy.

121
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,860
Like us?

122
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,230
No, not like us.

123
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:00,510
Creepy chummy,

124
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:02,250
like you and your dog.

125
00:05:02,990 --> 00:05:05,950
She feeds him out of her own mouth?

126
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:09,600
I mean, he calls her Debbie,

127
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,320
she calls him Stewie

128
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:13,610
and they're all giggly around each other.

129
00:05:13,610 --> 00:05:15,040
And believe me, when food goes in that mouth,

130
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:17,270
it does not come out.

131
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,180
So are you worried

132
00:05:19,180 --> 00:05:21,900
because he's replacing you as a son

133
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:24,770
or are you worried because he's becoming her lover?

134
00:05:24,770 --> 00:05:27,310
First of all, no one can replace me as a son.

135
00:05:27,310 --> 00:05:29,330
I'm her little matzo ball.

136
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:32,170
And secondly, my mother is well past

137
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:34,580
having any kind of sex life.

138
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:36,310
Okay, okay.

139
00:05:38,270 --> 00:05:40,100
Although many older women lead vibrant, active...

140
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,230
I said well past it!

141
00:05:45,730 --> 00:05:47,340
Excuse me, Officer Hernandez?

142
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:50,490
Any leads on the person who stole my belongings?

143
00:05:50,490 --> 00:05:51,160
Not yet.

144
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,840
Well, perhaps I can help.

145
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,950
Sherlock Holmes always says

146
00:05:55,650 --> 00:05:57,750
when you eliminate the impossible,

147
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:00,040
whatever remains, however improbable,

148
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,340
must be the truth.

149
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:04,320
Now, have-have you tried doing that?

150
00:06:05,290 --> 00:06:06,710
Nope.

151
00:06:07,370 --> 00:06:09,520
Well, maybe you should.

152
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,840
Th-Th-There's lots of books called "Sherlock Holmes"

153
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:15,850
and there's no books called "Officer Hernandez."

154
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,000
Thanks again for coming.

155
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,760
Six hours was gonna be a long drive by myself.

156
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,070
My pleasure.

157
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,130
And I'm not angry at all

158
00:06:30,130 --> 00:06:32,480
that my boyfriend was in trouble and called you instead of me.

159
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,110
I love that!

160
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:39,420
Yeah, time's gonna fly by.

161
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:44,060
I haven't been on a job interview in years.

162
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:45,190
I'm really nervous.

163
00:06:45,190 --> 00:06:46,230
Don't be.

164
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:48,110
You are built for pharmaceutical sales.

165
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:50,980
You're cute, you're flirty and...

166
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:53,620
Started that like there were gonna be three things.

167
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:58,080
I don't have any experience in sales.

168
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,230
Unless you count the bikini car wash I did in high school.

169
00:07:00,230 --> 00:07:03,030
But you already made me take that off my resume?

170
00:07:04,210 --> 00:07:06,350
This job is a lot like being a waitress,

171
00:07:06,350 --> 00:07:08,350
except instead of pushing the fish tacos

172
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:09,600
'cause they're about to go bad,

173
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,200
you're just pushing our antidepressants

174
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:15,350
before the FDA finds out they may cause rectal bleeding.

175
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:17,720
They do?

176
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,770
Maybe.

177
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,890
But like our lawyers say, the world is full of things

178
00:07:22,890 --> 00:07:25,110
that can cause a rectum to bleed.

179
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,520
Anyway, I talked you up to Dan.

180
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:30,050
He's the guy who'll be interviewing you.

181
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:31,450
Oh, I really appreciate this.

182
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:33,160
I just hope I'm not in over my head.

183
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,090
You'll be fine. Just be yourself.

184
00:07:35,090 --> 00:07:36,730
- I wish I felt more confident. - Penny,

185
00:07:36,730 --> 00:07:38,290
I wouldn't have put you up for this job

186
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,530
if I didn't think you could handle it.

187
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,830
Oh, thank you, but maybe I should cancel.

188
00:07:41,830 --> 00:07:43,730
It's too late to cancel. You're going.

189
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:45,570
But I don't know anything about pharmaceuticals.

190
00:07:45,570 --> 00:07:47,000
Oh, I understand.

191
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:49,640
You want to do something you're already good at.

192
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,420
I know.

193
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:51,330
Why don't I get you a job at

194
00:07:51,330 --> 00:07:55,000
the Sitting Around All Day Wearing Yoga Pants Factory?

195
00:07:58,890 --> 00:08:01,080
They're comfortable.

196
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:06,570
Ma, I hope you're decent. Raj is here!

197
00:08:06,570 --> 00:08:07,920
You just started seeing naked women again,

198
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:09,260
and I don't want you to be confused

199
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:11,040
about where the boobs should be.

200
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:14,390
Oh, hey, guys.

201
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:15,590
What are you doing here?

202
00:08:15,590 --> 00:08:18,050
Uh... w-what are you doing here?

203
00:08:18,050 --> 00:08:19,170
I thought you moved out.

204
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,100
Oh, yeah, I was going to,

205
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,880
and then Debbie and I got to talking

206
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:24,200
over dinner the other night.

207
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,730
I didn't have anyplace to go,

208
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:27,170
she likes having me around,

209
00:08:27,170 --> 00:08:30,390
so we both said, "Why leave?" at the same time.

210
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,400
It was precious.

211
00:08:34,590 --> 00:08:36,580
It's not that precious.

212
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,120
I'd like to back you up,

213
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:40,840
but it sounds like it was pretty precious.

214
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,800
Stewie, I can't find my glasses!

215
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:50,320
Be right there, Deb Deb!

216
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:52,830
They're probably on her head.

217
00:08:54,010 --> 00:08:56,310
Or in her neck. Listen.

218
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:00,110
You staying here seems like something

219
00:09:00,110 --> 00:09:02,170
she would've talked to me about.

220
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:06,100
Well, maybe if you called your mother more often, you'd know.

221
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:10,910
It wouldn't kill you to pick up the phone.

222
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,360
Any word on my stolen items?

223
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,230
We're doing everything we can.

224
00:09:31,290 --> 00:09:32,710
You know, Sherlock Holmes

225
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:35,680
liked to use cocaine to sharpen his focus.

226
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:41,470
But I'm sure those Cool Ranch Doritos are doing the trick.

227
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,250
Sheldon.

228
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:45,790
Leonard!

229
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:48,210
Oh, I'm so happy to see you.

230
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:50,570
- Are you okay? - Oh, I'm fine.

231
00:09:50,570 --> 00:09:52,910
Why did you come?

232
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:55,560
What do you mean, why did I come?

233
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:56,340
You're my boyfriend.

234
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:58,220
I haven't seen you in over a month.

235
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,260
I just drove six hours to help you out.

236
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,480
Don't you have anything to say besides,

237
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,490
"Why did you come?"

238
00:10:04,150 --> 00:10:05,580
I do, but...

239
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:07,400
I feel uncomfortable saying it out loud

240
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,820
in front of these police officers.

241
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:11,820
Fine.

242
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:13,150
Whisper it.

243
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,280
Shotgun.

244
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,870
So, Sheldon, tell us about your trip.

245
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,010
Where'd you go?

246
00:10:31,010 --> 00:10:32,450
Where didn't I go?

247
00:10:32,450 --> 00:10:34,800
I went to New York, Chicago,

248
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:38,080
Atlanta, Denver, Seattle.

249
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,320
How were they?

250
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,810
Oh, I have no idea.

251
00:10:40,810 --> 00:10:43,320
I never left the train station.

252
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:46,410
Hang on. You traveled across the entire country

253
00:10:46,410 --> 00:10:48,310
and never left a train station?

254
00:10:48,310 --> 00:10:49,700
Why would I?

255
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:51,970
That's where all the cool trains are.

256
00:10:53,090 --> 00:10:55,530
I'm sorry, so you never went outside?

257
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:58,230
Or had a single piece of fruit.

258
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,530
So...

259
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:03,630
why do you think you'd make

260
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:07,210
a good pharmaceutical sales rep?

261
00:11:07,210 --> 00:11:09,160
Well, I'm a people person.

262
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,080
People like me.

263
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,120
Some of my favorite people are people.

264
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:15,120
I feel like I'm saying "people" a lot.

265
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:17,580
People, people, people, pe... Okay, I'm done.

266
00:11:18,570 --> 00:11:19,720
You sure?

267
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,720
People. Yes.

268
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:23,820
Good!

269
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:26,580
So, how do you feel your previous job experience

270
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:29,590
has prepared you for a career like this?

271
00:11:29,590 --> 00:11:32,710
Uh, well, as a waitress, sales was a big part of my job.

272
00:11:32,710 --> 00:11:35,300
I mean, believe me, I convinced a lot of very large customers,

273
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,770
who should not be eating cheesecake,

274
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:38,610
to have more cheesecake.

275
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,240
I mean,

276
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:42,850
one of those chubsters even had an insulin pump!

277
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:48,410
I have an insulin pump.

278
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:53,220
People.

279
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,370
It's weird, right?

280
00:11:57,370 --> 00:12:00,740
A grown man in his 30s living with my mother.

281
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:02,070
That is weird.

282
00:12:02,070 --> 00:12:04,540
I thought he was, like, 45.

283
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,880
Come on, you don't think it's a little odd?

284
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:09,370
I don't know! I mean, she's lonely.

285
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:10,830
He needs a place to stay.

286
00:12:10,830 --> 00:12:12,820
I doubt there's any funny business going on.

287
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:14,420
And even if there was, who cares?

288
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,460
They're both adults.

289
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:16,900
"Who cares"?! You wouldn't care

290
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:18,990
if I slept with your mom?

291
00:12:18,990 --> 00:12:20,790
You know what? You're my best friend,

292
00:12:20,790 --> 00:12:21,860
and she's in a bad marriage.

293
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:24,110
I give you my blessing.

294
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:26,260
This is stupid.

295
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:29,790
I'm just gonna call my mother and be honest with her.

296
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,410
'Cause that's what little matzo balls do.

297
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:37,640
This is Debbie!

298
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:39,060
And this is Stuart!

299
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:43,030
Just kidding!

300
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,920
Leave a message!

301
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:52,070
This is the part where you talk.

302
00:12:54,590 --> 00:12:56,810
All right, let's say a physician was prescribing

303
00:12:56,810 --> 00:12:58,660
one of our competitor's drugs.

304
00:12:58,660 --> 00:13:01,320
How would you convince them to switch to ours?

305
00:13:08,170 --> 00:13:11,880
Any chance his car needs to be washed by a girl in a bikini?

306
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:15,480
No...

307
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,070
Okay, I'm really sorry for wasting your time.

308
00:13:18,070 --> 00:13:20,890
Don't worry about it. Thanks for stopping by.

309
00:13:20,890 --> 00:13:22,930
Okay, thanks.

310
00:13:24,310 --> 00:13:27,290
Um, I'm sor... listen, could you do me a favor

311
00:13:27,290 --> 00:13:30,160
and not tell Bernadette how badly I blew this interview?

312
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:31,390
She'll get upset.

313
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:34,840
And honestly I'm a... a little terrified of her.

314
00:13:37,450 --> 00:13:38,860
Wait, wait. You're scared of Bernadette?

315
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,730
Yeah, kind of.

316
00:13:40,730 --> 00:13:43,520
I thought it was just me!

317
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:47,330
E-Everyone thinks she's so nice

318
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:50,010
with that squeaky little voice.

319
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,700
I know, but she's kind of a bully!

320
00:13:53,230 --> 00:13:54,260
She is!

321
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:56,170
I-I didn't even want to meet you,

322
00:13:56,170 --> 00:13:59,710
but, uh, I was too scared to say no to her.

323
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:01,490
Me, too!

324
00:14:01,490 --> 00:14:03,070
Yeah, yeah! One-one time, I had...

325
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:04,670
Oh! I had to tell her

326
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:06,260
we were cutting the-the research funding

327
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:07,960
for one of the drugs she was developing.

328
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:09,200
What happened?

329
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:10,940
I couldn't do it!

330
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:12,420
She's still working on it!

331
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,240
We're not gonna tell her about this, right?

332
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:21,490
- Oh, my God, no! - No, no...

333
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:25,340
At the hot dog stand in the Denver train station--

334
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:26,630
Heinz ketchup.

335
00:14:26,630 --> 00:14:29,520
At the hot dog stand in the Salt Lake City train station--

336
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:30,970
Heinz ketchup.

337
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:34,460
At the hot dog stand in the Indianapolis train station...

338
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:38,110
I don't care.

339
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:41,900
Wrong! Hunt's!

340
00:14:43,530 --> 00:14:44,930
Hey, Amy! What do you say?

341
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:47,240
You ready to move on to the mustard round?

342
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:49,800
Have you not noticed that I've been sitting back here

343
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:53,080
quietly stewing for the past two hours?

344
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:56,090
I just thought you were bad at the game.

345
00:14:57,310 --> 00:14:59,060
I'm mad at you!

346
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,010
How could you just go away like that

347
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:02,360
without even saying good-bye,

348
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:05,110
and then call Leonard for help instead of me?

349
00:15:07,690 --> 00:15:08,950
Amy?

350
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:10,940
May I please have a moment of privacy

351
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:13,320
to speak with my roommate?

352
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:16,060
We're in a moving car!

353
00:15:18,350 --> 00:15:19,500
What do you expect me to do?

354
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,790
Stick my fingers in my ears?

355
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:23,760
Well, I was thinking put your head out the window like a dog,

356
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,230
but that'll work.

357
00:15:25,990 --> 00:15:28,040
Please? This'll be quick.

358
00:15:32,910 --> 00:15:34,010
Leonard?

359
00:15:34,010 --> 00:15:35,940
As soon as we get home,

360
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:38,650
I want to have coitus with Amy.

361
00:15:45,730 --> 00:15:47,480
Okay, she can't hear.

362
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,920
The reason I called you

363
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:54,420
is because I didn't want Amy

364
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:57,470
to know I couldn't make it on my own.

365
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,320
What's the big deal?

366
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,740
Oh, of course it's no big deal to you.

367
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:04,180
You idolize me, and nothing could ever knock me

368
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:06,450
off that pedestal you put me on.

369
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:08,260
Well, yeah, it's true.

370
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:10,320
You-you are a god to me.

371
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,210
Can I stop now?

372
00:16:13,210 --> 00:16:14,980
Just tell her.

373
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:19,980
I called Leonard because...

374
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,110
I failed.

375
00:16:21,110 --> 00:16:25,390
And I didn't want you to think less of me.

376
00:16:25,390 --> 00:16:27,970
You were worried about that?

377
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,750
Yes.

378
00:16:33,430 --> 00:16:35,280
Sheldon...

379
00:16:36,170 --> 00:16:39,560
it's okay with me that you're not perfect.

380
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:46,790
Can I have one more moment with Leonard?

381
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:48,870
Sure.

382
00:16:55,850 --> 00:16:58,650
Amy just hurt my feelings. I want to break up with her.

383
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:04,620
Now, I never thought I'd say this,

384
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:07,270
but I'm kind of excited to see Sheldon.

385
00:17:07,910 --> 00:17:11,210
I never thought I'd say this, but Penny got a job today.

386
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:13,380
She did?

387
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:14,990
Well, the only reason she got it

388
00:17:14,990 --> 00:17:17,750
is 'cause the guy who interviewed her loves me.

389
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:26,190
What do you want?

390
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:28,680
I, uh, kind of got the feeling

391
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:31,800
you might not be okay with me staying at your mom's.

392
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,310
You're right, I'm not.

393
00:17:33,310 --> 00:17:34,760
I think it's weird.

394
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:35,390
Howie?

395
00:17:35,390 --> 00:17:36,400
It is. He's a grown man.

396
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,510
He's just gonna live there rent-free?

397
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:39,880
How is that gonna motivate him

398
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:41,880
to get off his butt and get a job?

399
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:44,510
I mean, do you even have a plan?

400
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:46,940
Hey, you're not my father, okay?

401
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:49,090
And besides, your mother and I were talking...

402
00:17:49,090 --> 00:17:51,730
"Your mother and I"? You're not my father!

403
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:53,440
- I didn't say I was your father! - Well, I didn't say

404
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,290
- I was your father! - Okay, calm down.

405
00:17:55,290 --> 00:17:57,030
You're not his father, he's not your father!

406
00:17:57,030 --> 00:17:59,750
Nobody's anybody's father.

407
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:02,090
I-I'm sorry you don't like my life choices,

408
00:18:02,090 --> 00:18:03,070
but it's my life!

409
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:05,500
Well, it's my house, it's my rules!

410
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:07,810
Okay, Dad!

411
00:18:07,810 --> 00:18:10,100
If I mow the lawn, can I have my allowance?

412
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:12,300
Hey, don't you take that sarcastic tone with him!

413
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,550
I don't have to listen to you!

414
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,770
Don't talk to her like that!

415
00:18:14,770 --> 00:18:16,450
That is my mother... Wife!

416
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:18,670
My wife! I said my wife!

417
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:19,900
You know what?

418
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,560
This isn't getting us anywhere.

419
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:24,610
When you're ready to apologize, you know where to find me.

420
00:18:24,610 --> 00:18:26,430
Well, yeah, in my house!

421
00:18:26,430 --> 00:18:28,800
That's right, sucka!

422
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,430
I wish I'd never gone on that trip.

423
00:18:34,430 --> 00:18:37,000
I feel no better now than when I left.

424
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,570
But you still accomplished something.

425
00:18:38,570 --> 00:18:40,270
Yeah. If you had told anyone

426
00:18:40,270 --> 00:18:43,320
that you were going away on a train by yourself across the country,

427
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,040
do you know what they would have said?

428
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,080
- That I couldn't do it? - Exactly.

429
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,540
Right after they said, "Yay!"

430
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:52,610
But you did do it.

431
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:54,680
So what if it didn't all go your way?

432
00:18:54,690 --> 00:18:56,950
That's what makes it an adventure.

433
00:18:56,950 --> 00:18:59,050
That's a good point.

434
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:02,140
Yeah, I'm a lot like Gandalf the Grey.

435
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:04,930
He fought the Balrog and emerged

436
00:19:04,930 --> 00:19:07,570
stronger than ever as Gandalf the White.

437
00:19:07,570 --> 00:19:10,190
I was robbed of my phone and pants,

438
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:12,530
and I, too, came back stronger.

439
00:19:12,530 --> 00:19:13,710
And whiter, too,

440
00:19:13,710 --> 00:19:16,340
'cause I wasn't in direct sunlight for six weeks.

441
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:20,470
See? This trip was good for you.

442
00:19:20,470 --> 00:19:21,790
Indeed.

443
00:19:21,790 --> 00:19:25,250
I was the world's smartest caterpillar.

444
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:28,790
And then after pupating in our nation's railway system,

445
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:30,400
I've burst forth

446
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:33,600
as the world's smartest butterfly.

447
00:19:34,690 --> 00:19:37,360
Butterfly could've gotten himself home from Arizona.

448
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:41,520
Yeah, I feel renewed.

449
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:45,020
I'm ready to deal with any changes that come my way.

450
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:48,310
Look who's back!

451
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:50,010
Your hair is different. You changed your hair.

452
00:19:50,010 --> 00:19:51,860
I can't take this. I'm out.

453
00:19:57,390 --> 00:19:59,460
Would you like to see pictures from my trip?

454
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:00,890
I thought your phone got stolen.

455
00:20:00,890 --> 00:20:02,810
Yeah, it did, but luckily all my photos

456
00:20:02,810 --> 00:20:04,700
got backed up to the Cloud.

457
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:07,540
And you thought they all had a silver lining.

458
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,340
Here-- day one.

459
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:11,860
Uh, this was the seat I was going to sit

460
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:12,780
in but didn't

461
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:15,500
because there were cracker crumbs on it.

462
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:19,330
As it was first class, I suspect Ritz.

463
00:20:20,290 --> 00:20:23,050
This is the train bathroom.

464
00:20:23,050 --> 00:20:25,080
This is the Imodium I took

465
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:28,180
so I would never have to use the train bathroom.

466
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:30,700
I cannot believe you traveled the entire country

467
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,390
and never left the train station.

468
00:20:32,390 --> 00:20:33,410
I know.

469
00:20:33,410 --> 00:20:35,740
You know, I almost died in a fire in Des Moines,

470
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,580
but I stayed put.

471
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:39,310
FYI--

472
00:20:39,310 --> 00:20:41,750
that's when the Imodium gave out.

